            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "By default, 'mini.animate' implements resizing animation (for example, type `<C-w>|` in vertical split and then `<C-w>=`). This also applies to resizing with mouse.\r\n\r\nIf I use mouse in an attempt for a quick (almost instant) resize, then it seems that Neovim registers it as a single resize and applies animation (although it might depend on the terminal emulator). If I move mouse slightly slower, then border more or less follows the mouse.\r\n\r\nIf you don't like this effect, either adjust [timing of resizing](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/c3b37f4afb933141a750b60b86fb6ef6b50d0e61/doc/mini-animate.txt#L360-L361) (for your use case linear easing with `unit = 'step'` and duration about 10 might be a better alternative) or disable `resize` animation completely.\r\n\r\nClosing as an intended behavior with 'mini.animate'.",
